2|0@television^1438978870#ctv73kn:irishgirlie33$:This is the first thing I remember watching, outside of network news coverage. I was a hot mess at the time, coping with loss of my brother's girlfriend on the first plane, trying to process what was going on in NYC and someone came over to my apartment to check on me and flipped on the daily show. Jon Stewart started talking, being honest and emotional. It took me 12 years to watch it again, because the pain of that day is still inside me, he was so eloquent and real. I watched it again yesterday, and it was like the first time. Thank you, Jon Stewart, for everything. 
