5|0@television^1438948761#ctuouf3:Legless1234$:I'm a Brit and I'll never forget that day of infamy. And I'll never forget my reaction to it. I didn't know I was capable of so much rage, so much hate. If I had my way, that day, the Middle East would have been a sea of glass. I would have nuked their arses back to the stone age. I would have murderd millions of innocents to try and satisfy my desire for payback, for revenge. I'm so glad I wasn't in charge. Today, l have a fair number of Muslim friends. I've been to birthday parties for their kids, they've been to my house for barbecues. We have fun and respect each others beliefs. But, on that day, I turned into a monster. I wish I'd had the opportunity to watch that clip back then. It might have helped me deal with the pain I felt for people I'd never met, people I didn't know. People who didn't deserve to meet their death that day. Since this has now turned into a ramble about 9/11 instead of Jon, I'd like to end by talking about your police, firefighters and first responders. The guys who were rushing into the towers while everyone else was running out. The men and women who marched to the sound of the guns. There's a special place for you in Heaven, Valhalla. 
